    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0129" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1948v01p1/pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC/8–1448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in France </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-08-18T16:00:00-04:00">August 18, 1948—4
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3182. We are following suggestion last para urtel 4214 Aug 14,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d58-f1"/> and approaching Benelux countries. Please inform French,
                    while we have no objection their further discussion matter Benelux, we would
                    prefer our position not be mentioned by them pending opportunity for us to
                    consult on matter wider basis. For your info Brit have not given us definite
                    indication their thinking, although have implied Norway might become their first
                    choice.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d58-f1" n="1" xml:id="d58-f1-content">
                <p>Officials at the French Foreign Ministry had expressed a desire to inform the
                    Benelux countries of the United States position regarding the Security Council
                    seat being vacated by Belgium, namely that it was impractical to support the
                    candidacy of Luxembourg for this seat (501.BC/8–1448).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
